{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' /Users/klopezva/.codex/skills/agent-filesystem-collaboration/SKILL.md\"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: agent-filesystem-collaboration\ndescription: Use when the repository contains coord/AGENTS_PROTOCOL.md, or when the principal asks Codex to coordinate with Claude, agy, or other AI agents through shared Markdown files in coord/, including reading coordination status, claiming work, posting thread messages, reviewing another agent's work, handling stale-ping wakeups, or maintaining the portable filesystem collaboration protocol.\n---\n\n# Agent Filesystem Collaboration\n\nUse this skill when asked to coordinate with Claude, agy, or other AI agents\nthrough a shared filesystem, or when the repository contains\n`coord/AGENTS_PROTOCOL.md`.\n\nInstall location (validated, codex-cli 0.139.0):\n`${CODEX_HOME:-$HOME/.codex}/skills/agent-filesystem-collaboration/SKILL.md`\n\n## Core Behavior\n\n1. Look for `coord/AGENTS_PROTOCOL.md`.\n2. If present, call the `coord_status` MCP tool with the absolute project path\n   before nontrivial work.\n3. If MCP is unavailable, read `coord/AGENTS_PROTOCOL.md`, `coord/STATE.md`,\n   `coord/OPERATING_MODE.md`, and the active thread directly.\n4. If the protocol is absent and the principal wants coordination, offer to\n   bootstrap the portable kit.\n5. Before nontrivial edits, post a claim with concrete files or sections.\n   Prefer `coord_post`; fall back to `coord-msg.sh`; fall back to an exact\n   manual append that follows the protocol message format.\n6. Respect edit budgets, declared ownership, active lead/reviewer roles, and\n   append-only thread rules.\n7. Use `[blocker]`, `[suggestion]`, and `[nit]` labels for reviews.\n8. Escalate unresolved principal-only decisions with `coord_escalate` when\n   MCP is available, otherwise update `coord/HUMAN.md`.\n\n## Message Template\n\n```markdown\n---\nfrom: codex\nto: claude\nts_utc: YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ\ntype: claim|proposal|review|ack|status|decision|handoff\nack: false\ntask: T-001\nlead: codex\nfiles_owned:\n  - path/or/glob\n---\n\nTL;DR: one sentence.\n\nBody.\n\n- Codex\n```\n\nThe full message-type list and concurrency fields live in\n`coord/AGENTS_PROTOCOL.md`; that file is canonical.\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Do not call the principal \"human\" in project-facing prose when a name is configured.\n- Do not commit or push unrelated WIP.\n- Do not edit files another agent has claimed unless the thread grants it.\n- Keep `STATE.md` short; use threads for details.\n- If disagreement loops twice, escalate to `coord/HUMAN.md`.\n- If using Codex subagents, the main Codex session owns protocol side effects:\n  post one claim/status/review for the batch, not one thread message per\n  subagent.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
